        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "The read-only review found a late cost event for **work order MO-25-09-1070** (ID **WO-2025-09-004**):\n\n- **Source transaction:** `TXN-ISSUE-250930-1070` (component issue; event `CE-250904-0004`)\n- **Amount:** **$284,763.42** (28,476,342 cents)\n- **Event created:** **2025-09-30 19:15:00**\n- **September Pending Close entered:** **2025-09-30 18:00:00**\n- **Time late:** **75 minutes**\n- **Recorded accounting status:** **POSTED**\n\n**Conclusion:** The recorded status is **not consistent** with Oracle’s documented Pending Close treatment. Oracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B says newly created transactions falling in or before a Pending Close period are not staged for accounting until the period is closed or reopened. This was an INPUT/component-issue event created after Pending Close; it is not one of the stated continuing-processing exceptions.\n\nThe report was submitted and verified. No database records were changed.",
